hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17091","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting. He said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' wrote to me, and in his book was: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Yazid ibn al-Akhnas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no rivalry among you except in two: a man to whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave the Qur'an, so he stands with it by night and by day and follows what is in it, so a man says: If only Allah Almighty had given me like what He gave so-and-so, so I would stand with it as he stands with it; and a man to whom Allah gave wealth, so he spends and gives charity, so a man says: If only Allah had given me like what He gave so-and-so, so I would give charity with it. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what of bravery in a man? And the remainder of the hadith is missing."
